{"availability":"available","full":"jcfigueiredo/evem","name":"evem","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2023-12-06T21:28:46Z","updated":"2026-10-06T02:47:00Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://jcfigueiredo.github.io/evem/playground/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:01.154Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:01.154Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:01.154Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T02:36:01.154Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small TypeScript event emitter with wildcards, priorities, middleware, flow control, schema validation and history, plus optional WebSocket and Server-Sent Events adapters. No dependencies; ESM; Node.js 22+ and modern browsers.","Showcase · Playground (try every feature against the real library) · Documentation · Changelog"],"features":["Events: dot-separated names and wildcard patterns (user., .created), priorities, once-only subscriptions, and cancelable events. Async subscribers are awaited one after the other, in priority order.","Subscription options: filters (sync or async), throttle and debounce, transforms that pass changed data to the next subscribers, and schema validation.","Middleware: see every event first, for all events or by pattern, to change its data, send it under another name, or cancel it.","Errors, timeouts and recursion: per-publish error policies, a timeout for each async subscriber, and a limit on events that re-publish themselves.","History and debugging: record events and replay them to late subscribers, get a warning when subscriptions pile up, and inspect everything with info()."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jcfigueiredo/evem/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"342c6cdce5f7a80ee2f016cd134b55b9bd552aae3aeea2b55e36f20492eb9d83","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T02:36:01.383Z"},"overv